For control.c nonce construction: put session as big-endian u64 in bytes
0-7, then (sequence << 1 | (kind == REPLY ? 1 : 0)) as big-endian u32
in bytes 8-11. Use cpu_to_be64/cpu_to_be32 (kernel) or manual byte
packing (userspace).

For open_request: parse the 18-byte header first (version, kind, session,
sequence). Verify version == RK_SECURE_VERSION, kind == REQUEST, session
matches channel->session, and sequence == channel->next_request. Build
the nonce from session + sequence + REQUEST, then call rk_aead_open()
with the header as AAD. On success, increment next_request.

For seal_reply: build the header with version, REPLY, session,
next_reply. Build the nonce from session + next_reply + REPLY. Call
rk_aead_seal() with header as AAD and plaintext as message. On success,
increment next_reply.

For agent.c rk_agent_reply: seal plaintext with rk_secure_seal_reply()
into an envelope buffer, then rk_send_frame() the envelope. Always
memzero_explicit() the envelope after sending.

For rk_agent_serve: generate a non-zero session with get_random_u64(),
start the secure channel, send sealed HELLO, then loop: receive frame,
rk_secure_open_request() to get plaintext, pass to rk_agent_command().
Stop channel on exit.
